WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.660
Your phone and your future: earn, learn and stay safe.

2
00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:10.580
This is the video for Module 4 of Smartphone and Digital Awareness: digital literacy and your future.

3
00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:19.760
A smartphone does not make money by itself. It helps you show what you sell, reach customers, take orders and receive payment.

4
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.130
It is also a classroom you can carry.

5
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.550
What you post builds trust, or costs you opportunities.

6
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.950
And you have rights online, just as you do offline. Let us see how to use all of this.

7
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:44.770
For example, Adunni in Ibadan makes plantain chips. She posts daylight photos with the price and how to order, and sells about 40 packs a week.

8
00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.540
Each pack sells for about 1,000 naira.

9
00:00:49.790 --> 00:00:53.700
Ingredients and packaging cost about 600 naira per pack.

10
00:00:54.950 --> 00:01:02.800
So she makes 400 naira on each pack. That is 16,000 naira a week, and 64,000 naira over 4 weeks.

11
00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:14.000
After about 5,000 naira for data, airtime and delivery, she earns about 59,000 naira a month. She records every sale, so she knows the real figure.

12
00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.430
Show your product clearly, with the price.

13
00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:23.780
Confirm every order in writing: item, quantity, total price and delivery day.

14
00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:31.880
The customer pays by bank transfer, or to a licensed provider such as Opay, Moniepoint or PalmPay.

15
00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:40.340
Now the most important step. Open your own bank or payment app, and see the money in your balance before you release goods.

16
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:46.770
Then deliver, and write the sale in your record: date, customer, item, amount, paid.

17
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:58.540
Genuine work pays you. Schemes take your money. Be suspicious if you must pay to join, if you earn by recruiting others, or if it promises to double your money.

18
00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:11.220
Watch out when you are paid small amounts for easy tasks, then asked to deposit more to unlock earnings. If you are caught, stop paying, keep screenshots, and call your bank on its official number.

19
00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:18.570
Your phone is a classroom. To save data, download lessons on Wi-Fi and watch them offline.

20
00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.490
Lower the video quality. For talking lessons, you lose little.

21
00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.770
Listen to talks as audio while you cook or travel.

22
00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:32.050
And read text lessons, which use far less data.

23
00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:45.160
Make study a fixed appointment. For example, Rahila in Jos studies 20 minutes a day, five days a week. She counts reading and practice time, so she plans 6 weeks for her course.

24
00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:56.760
Your NIN and BVN are keys to your identity and money. Never post photos of your NIN slip, ID card, passport or ATM card.

25
00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:08.350
For example, Chiamaka in Enugu searches her own name before a job application. She deletes an old angry post, and asks a friend to remove a photo of her ID card.

26
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:16.040
Then she uses the same name and a clear photo on WhatsApp and LinkedIn, with an honest one-line bio.

27
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:35.720
The Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 gives you rights over your personal data, enforced by the NDPC. For example, Ladi in Lafia keeps getting marketing calls. She emails the company, asks what data they hold, and asks them to stop marketing to her.

28
00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:40.000
She saves the email and writes the date in her notebook.

29
00:03:41.250 --> 00:03:44.280
The company replies and removes her from marketing.

30
00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:53.660
If it had not, she would complain to the NDPC through its official website. For network problems, go to the NCC.

31
00:03:54.910 --> 00:04:01.460
To remember. Confirm payment in your own app. Never pay to join a money scheme. Study at a fixed time.

32
00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:05.800
Keep ID documents off the internet, and use your rights in writing.

33
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:12.080
Finally, write a 30-day plan with three SMART goals: safety, organisation and growth.

34
00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:21.780
In this module you will make a phone-earning plan, set a study routine, check your footprint, practise your rights, and write your 30-day plan.

35
00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.070
Continue with the lessons below.
